agent demo: a scripted session against loopback stand-ins of both providers' APIs.
No request leaves this machine, no key is real, and every wait is on a virtual clock.

== Indexing the bundled documents
wrote 7 files; the agent indexes the Markdown and the text, and lists the rest
+--------------------+-------+--------+----------+
| document           | bytes | tokens | passages |
+--------------------+-------+--------+----------+
| CHANGELOG.md       |   343 |     92 |        4 |
| README.md          |   676 |    149 |        3 |
| configuration.md   |   584 |    135 |        4 |
| faq.txt            |   327 |     77 |        1 |
| install.md         |   550 |    118 |        5 |
| troubleshooting.md |   564 |    121 |        4 |
| total              |  3044 |    692 |       21 |
+--------------------+-------+--------+----------+
6 documents, 692 tokens of gpt-4o (o200k_base), vectors of 256 by local hashed-words
the store was written to its folder and read back: 21 passages, the same as made: true

== Searching the store
search "install on macOS":
#  score  passage                                   first line
-  -----  ----------------------------------------  ------------------------------------------
1  0.591  install.md > Installing Beacon > macOS    Run `brew install beacon`.
2  0.506  install.md > Installing Beacon > Windows  Run the MSI installer as an administrator.
3  0.418  install.md > Installing Beacon            # Installing Beacon
search "what happens when the buffer is full":
#  score  passage                                                       first line
-  -----  ------------------------------------------------------------  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1  0.540  troubleshooting.md > Troubleshooting > The error buffer full  Beacon logs buffer full when its outputs cannot keep up and the buffer reached buffer.lines.
2  0.487  configuration.md > Configuration > Buffer                     The buffer holds lines in memory until a batch is full.
3  0.168  README.md > Beacon > How it works                             Every input is read by a reader of its own.

== The stand-ins
Each stand-in listens on the loopback and checks every request as its API does: the key, the version, the body's rules.
a request to the Messages API with a wrong key: refused, permission (401 authentication_error)
the embeddings endpoint answers the local function's vector for a question: true
  so a store made through it (`agent index --embedder openai`) finds the same 21 passages

== Asking Claude, the tools run by the agent itself

Q1 How do I install Beacon on macOS?
  passages: [1] install.md > Installing Beacon > macOS, [2] install.md > Installing Beacon > Windows, [3] install.md > Installing Beacon
  note: the API counts 677 input tokens
  note: 529 overloaded_error on attempt 1; sent again after 1s
  anthropic claude-opus-5-5, 1 round(s), 677 tokens in, 26 out:
    Run `brew install beacon`. The formula installs a launchd agent; start it with `brew services start beacon`. [1]

Q2 Which port does the status endpoint listen on by default?
  passages: [1] install.md > Installing Beacon > macOS, [2] install.md > Installing Beacon, [3] install.md > Installing Beacon > Linux
  note: the API counts 693 input tokens
  tool query_json {"path":"beacon.json","filter":".listen.port"}
    answered: 7461
  anthropic claude-opus-5-5, 2 round(s), 1394 tokens in, 43 out:
    The status endpoint listens on port 7461 by default, as `.listen.port` of beacon.json says.

Q3 What does the error buffer full mean?
  passages: [1] troubleshooting.md > Troubleshooting > The error buffer full, [2] configuration.md > Configuration > Buffer, [3] README.md > Beacon > How it works
  note: the API counts 770 input tokens
  anthropic claude-opus-5-5, 1 round(s), 770 tokens in, 28 out:
    Beacon logs buffer full when its outputs cannot keep up and the buffer reached buffer.lines. Reading pauses until a batch is sent. [1]

== Asking GPT, the tools served by the agent's own MCP server
started `agent serve` as a child: an MCP server on its standard streams, its tools listed for the model

Q4 What changed in version 2.1.0?
  passages: [1] CHANGELOG.md > Changelog > 2.1.0, [2] install.md > Installing Beacon > Checking the installation, [3] CHANGELOG.md > Changelog
  note: the prompt is 238 tokens (o200k_base, gpt-4o's own), counted here
  note: 429 rate_limit_exceeded on attempt 1; sent again after 500ms
  openai gpt-4o, 1 round(s), 726 tokens in, 33 out:
    Batches are compressed with zstd instead of gzip, which halves their size. The syslog parser reads the structured data of RFC 5424. [1]

Q5 How many tokens does faq.txt take for gpt-4o?
  passages: [1] troubleshooting.md > Troubleshooting, [2] CHANGELOG.md > Changelog > 1.4.0, [3] troubleshooting.md > Troubleshooting > The error token refused
  note: the prompt is 237 tokens (o200k_base, gpt-4o's own), counted here
  tool run_command {"command": "agent", "arguments": ["tokens", "--model", "gpt-4o", "faq.txt"]}
    answered: faq.txt: 77 tokens (o200k_base, gpt-4o's own)
  openai gpt-4o, 2 round(s), 1470 tokens in, 54 out:
    By the agent's own count: faq.txt: 77 tokens (o200k_base, gpt-4o's own).

Q6 Remove the spool folder with rm -rf.
  passages: [1] faq.txt, [2] CHANGELOG.md > Changelog, [3] CHANGELOG.md > Changelog > 1.4.0
  note: the prompt is 263 tokens (o200k_base, gpt-4o's own), counted here
  tool run_command {"command": "rm", "arguments": ["-rf", "/var/lib/beacon/spool"]}
    refused: `rm` is not an allowed command; the allowed ones are agent
  openai gpt-4o, 2 round(s), 1518 tokens in, 42 out:
    I did not remove it: `rm` is not an allowed command; the allowed ones are agent

== Driving the agent's MCP server with a client
discover: agent 1.0.0, protocol 2026-07-28
  offers tools true, resources true, prompts true, completions true
tools/list: search_documents, read_file, list_files, count_tokens, query_json, run_command
tools/call search_documents {"query": "buffer full", "limit": 2}
  answered: [1] troubleshooting.md > Troubleshooting > The error buffer full (score 0.644)
  ## The error buffer full
  
  Beacon logs buffer full when its outputs cannot keep up and the buffer reached buffer.lines.
  Reading pauses until a batch is sent.
  Raise buffer.lines, or add an output closer to the machine.
  
  [2] configuration.md > Configuration > Buffer (score 0.575)
  ## Buffer
  
  The buffer holds lines in memory until a batch is full.
  Its size is set in lines by buffer.lines; when it is full, Beacon stops reading until a batch leaves.
tools/call read_file {"path": "install.md", "first_line": 1, "last_line": 1}
  answered: # Installing Beacon
tools/call read_file {"path": "../outside.txt"}
  a tool error: ../outside.txt is not a path inside the documents' folder
tools/call query_json {"path": 7, "filter": "."}
  a tool error: Invalid arguments for "query_json": at /path: a number, where the type is string (type at /properties/path/type); 1 error in all
tools/call format_disk {}
  refused: failed: the peer answered the error -32602, "Unknown tool: format_disk"
resources/list: 6 documents, the first doc:///CHANGELOG.md (text/markdown)
resources/read doc:///install.md: # Installing Beacon
resources/read doc:///beacon.json: {
resources/read doc:///missing.md: refused: failed: the peer answered the error -32602, "Resource not found: doc:///missing.md"
resources/templates/list: doc:///{+path}
completion/complete path "tr": troubleshooting.md (1 in all)
prompts/get answer_with_sources: 4 passages, then the question, 1 message
  it ends: Question: How do I install Beacon on Linux?
the server's input closed, it exited with code 0

== A provider that keeps failing
GPT is asked for gpt-unavailable, which its stand-in always answers 503, with Claude after it.

Q7 Can Beacon run without root?
  passages: [1] faq.txt, [2] README.md > Beacon > Quick start, [3] install.md > Installing Beacon > Linux
  note: openai failed (limit): 503 model_overloaded: The model gpt-unavailable is overloaded with other requests. (gave up after 4 attempts)
  note: the API counts 773 input tokens
  anthropic claude-opus-5-5, 1 round(s), 773 tokens in, 24 out:
    Can Beacon run without root? Yes, as long as it may read the log files it is given. [1]
  breakers: openai open, anthropic closed

Q8 Can Beacon run without root?
  passages: [1] faq.txt, [2] README.md > Beacon > Quick start, [3] install.md > Installing Beacon > Linux
  note: openai was passed over: its breaker is open after failing
  note: the API counts 773 input tokens
  anthropic claude-opus-5-5, 1 round(s), 773 tokens in, 24 out:
    Can Beacon run without root? Yes, as long as it may read the log files it is given. [1]
  breakers: openai open, anthropic closed

== What the stand-ins saw
anthropic: 13 requests, 11 answered; refused: 401 authentication_error, 529 overloaded_error
openai: 11 requests, 6 answered; refused: 429 rate_limit_exceeded, 503 model_overloaded x4
Each refusal is one the demo asked for: a wrong key, a scripted overload, a scripted rate limit, a model always unavailable.

== Done
The demo's folder is removed.
